WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.068
-My first guest
is a three-time Emmy winner

00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:05.872
starring on the very popular
series "The Blacklist."

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:09.008
Season eight
premieres tomorrow at 8:00 p.m.

00:00:09.008 --> 00:00:10.776
right here on NBC.

00:00:10.776 --> 00:00:13.713
I am thrilled he's here tonight
actually in the studio.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.982
Please welcome James Spader!

00:00:15.982 --> 00:00:17.450
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.450 --> 00:00:18.851
-♪ Don't be a hater ♪

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:21.487
♪ It's time for James Spader ♪

00:00:21.487 --> 00:00:25.391
♪ It's been a while,
you've been missed ♪

00:00:25.391 --> 00:00:27.226
♪ You can thank me later ♪

00:00:27.226 --> 00:00:29.929
♪ It's time for James Spader ♪

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:34.167
♪ Ain't that the dude
from "Blacklist"? ♪

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.970
♪ James Spader,
time for James Spader ♪

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:41.507
-Come on, James Spader!

00:00:41.507 --> 00:00:44.744
Oh, my pal,
it's great to see you.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:48.948
And, yes, thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:51.383
You look fantastic, by the way.

00:00:51.383 --> 00:00:52.485
Thank you for dressing up.

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.919
You're wearing a suit.
You look great.

00:00:53.919 --> 00:00:56.523
-You're looking...less so.

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:58.157
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.157 --> 00:01:00.159
-This is the --
I'm more casual.

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:01.894
-Remember when it was
only California?

00:01:01.894 --> 00:01:04.364
-[ Laughing ]
No, it's everywhere now.

00:01:04.364 --> 00:01:05.898
-You could wear your Crocs.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:08.401
-I'm wearing, basically --
These are like --

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.169
These are Yeezys.

00:01:10.169 --> 00:01:12.905
-This is my first time out
in eight months.

00:01:12.905 --> 00:01:14.607
Truly.
-Wow!

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.576
I'm so happy that --
-You're my date night.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.912
-Yes! I will be -- We are
your best date you ever --

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:22.748
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:22.748 --> 00:01:24.751
-They don't have the sake?

00:01:24.751 --> 00:01:27.653
-Can we get a little sake
or something?

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.888
Is this -- I don't --

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:32.825
I couldn't even see you
if we did a Zoom interview.

00:01:32.825 --> 00:01:36.095
-No, no, no, I couldn't --
This was the only option.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:38.063
I don't know how the --
You know, I can't --

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:40.766
You know, I don't --
I've had a couple of times

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:42.902
over the last eight months of,

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:45.537
you know,
having to do, uh...something.

00:01:45.537 --> 00:01:48.507
I just call in on the phone.
-Yeah. Yeah, yeah.

00:01:48.507 --> 00:01:50.243
-I don't know
how to work any of the stuff.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.678
I don't have a laptop or a --
-Yeah.

00:01:52.678 --> 00:01:53.846
-I don't know
how to do any of it.

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:56.248
-Good, but that's you.
I would agree with that.

00:01:56.248 --> 00:01:57.417
I'd say, "No, I don't..."

00:01:57.417 --> 00:02:00.186
-And I also --
I'm not presentable at home.

00:02:00.186 --> 00:02:01.487
[ Laughter ]
-Really?

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:03.656
-You know, I really --
Not really.

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:06.626
I-I-I'm...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:09.229
I'm either in the kitchen,
cooking...

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:12.298
-Yeah.
-...or -- If I'm in the house,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.802
I'm either in the kitchen,
cooking, or in the bathroom...

00:02:15.802 --> 00:02:17.770
-Mm-hmm, yes.
-Or...

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.973
[ Laughter ]
-Cooking.

00:02:19.973 --> 00:02:22.208
-Or in bed.
-Cooking. There you go.

00:02:22.208 --> 00:02:24.210
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:26.179
Yeah, that's true.
So, yeah, don't --

00:02:26.179 --> 00:02:28.781
My thing is that everyone wants
to do Zoom everything now.

00:02:28.781 --> 00:02:31.150
So, whatever it is,
they go, "Zoom call?"

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.384
I go, "No,
you don't have to Zoom."

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:34.520
-Yeah, but I worry
that we've got to come back

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.289
from this at some point.
You know?

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:40.025
Like, I was watching
the beginning of the show

00:02:40.025 --> 00:02:43.729
in the dressing room.
And, you know --

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:45.365
there are a lot
of people missing.

00:02:45.365 --> 00:02:47.132
Not just audience.
But there are a lot of people

00:02:47.132 --> 00:02:48.534
missing, in terms of...
-Yeah.

00:02:48.534 --> 00:02:50.503
-...you know, the functioning
of the show and so on.

00:02:50.503 --> 00:02:54.674
-Yes, yeah.
-And we can't let

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:56.976
the powers that be
think that this is

00:02:56.976 --> 00:02:58.578
what it's gonna be
moving forward,

00:02:58.578 --> 00:03:00.212
that it's gonna be, like --

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:02.047
You know, we don't want
to get them used to --

00:03:02.047 --> 00:03:04.917
We don't want NBC to get used
to a skeleton crew.

00:03:04.917 --> 00:03:06.752
-No, exactly right.
We got to get back.

00:03:06.752 --> 00:03:09.188
We got to get back.
Exactly right.

00:03:09.188 --> 00:03:11.123
This helps us, you being here.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:11.123 --> 00:03:14.193
-Yeah.
-Yeah, I -- What would it be --

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:17.496
What was your life like
in quarantine?

00:03:17.496 --> 00:03:19.465
-[ Laughing ]
-I'm trying to picture it.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.602
-'Cause I -- you know, they had
asked at one point whether --

00:03:22.602 --> 00:03:24.303
'Cause you and I
were supposed to do a show...

00:03:24.303 --> 00:03:26.839
-That's right, in March.
-...when it got shut down, yeah.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:30.042
And I think it was
a little later, maybe.

00:03:30.042 --> 00:03:33.379
I can't remember.
But anyway, it didn't work out.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:35.948
And I think that --
I think I got asked

00:03:35.948 --> 00:03:39.252
at some point during lockdown,

00:03:39.252 --> 00:03:41.888
or you were doing the show
from your home.

00:03:41.888 --> 00:03:43.622
-Yep.
-And I think I got asked

00:03:43.622 --> 00:03:45.758
whether I'd be interested
in doing it,

00:03:45.758 --> 00:03:47.927
and I was like,
"You know, forget that."

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:50.396
-You can't do it, no.
-But I tuned in to see --

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.564
And, you know,
it was a Herculean effort.

00:03:52.564 --> 00:03:53.966
I mean...
-Thank you.

00:03:53.966 --> 00:03:58.037
-...it really, truly,
for everyone who, you know --

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.538
-I tried.
-I mean, really.

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:02.007
You know, and, uh...

00:04:02.007 --> 00:04:05.044
I thought that was very
industrious and impressive.

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:08.180
You know, that slide?
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:11.150
-Yeah. I have a slide.
-How did you do that?

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.619
-You have to have a slide
in your house.

00:04:12.619 --> 00:04:13.953
Yeah, that's the one thing --
Yeah.

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.355
-That would not go well
with my hangover.

00:04:16.355 --> 00:04:17.857
[ Laughter ]

00:04:17.857 --> 00:04:20.192
-No, it makes it so much easier
to get to the kitchen, yeah.

00:04:20.192 --> 00:04:21.427
To have breakfast,
you just slide down.

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:23.629
-Anyway, so you're doing that.
Other people --

00:04:23.629 --> 00:04:26.666
Like, John Krasinski, like,
invented a network.

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:28.634
-Yeah, that's right,
that's right, he did, yeah.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:30.469
-You know?
And I came back to work, like,

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:33.773
my first day back --
back at work,

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:36.709
Christine Bean --
great costume designer

00:04:36.709 --> 00:04:42.648
we have on the show --
she conceived and grew

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:46.685
a whole human being
during this eight months.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.855
I came in for my fitting,
and she was just, like,

00:04:49.855 --> 00:04:52.124
heading out the door
to go have the baby.

00:04:52.124 --> 00:04:55.527
And when we left in March,
she wasn't pregnant at all.

00:04:55.527 --> 00:04:57.763
So, I mean,
what use of time is that?

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.099
-Yes.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.099 --> 00:05:03.836
-And then, my first day filming,
Megan Boone...

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:05.437
-Yeah.
-...who's on the show...

00:05:05.437 --> 00:05:08.374
-Of course.
-I said, "So, how have you been?

00:05:08.374 --> 00:05:11.544
What did you do
during the time off?"

00:05:11.544 --> 00:05:15.615
She said, "I read all
of Shakespeare's tragedies."

00:05:15.615 --> 00:05:17.049
-Wow.

00:05:17.049 --> 00:05:18.384
And what was your answer?

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:22.221
What did you do
during quarantine?

00:05:22.221 --> 00:05:25.357
-My youngest son,
my 12-year-old,

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:29.595
we'd go out
and line up beer cans

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:35.134
on the big rock out on
the far end of the garden

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:37.303
and shoot at them with BB guns.

00:05:37.303 --> 00:05:39.905
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:41.907
-So, someone had a baby.
[ Applause ]

00:05:41.907 --> 00:05:44.844
Someone read all
of Shakespeare's tragedies.

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.146
And you shot beer cans
with a BB gun.

00:05:47.146 --> 00:05:49.414
-And we'd throw the ball.
-[ Laughing ] Yeah.

00:05:49.414 --> 00:05:51.617
-You look great.
-Thank you.

00:05:51.617 --> 00:05:54.420
-Yeah, Questlove looks great.
Yeah, thank you.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:57.457
Also, I worked out a little bit
over the --

00:05:57.457 --> 00:05:58.724
-You did?

00:05:58.724 --> 00:06:00.826
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.826 --> 00:06:03.529
-More with James Spader
when we come back, everybody.

